  "worked_solution": "De Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\phi )]^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(n\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=5$ and $\\phi =\\sqrt{5}\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\sqrt{5}\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\sqrt{5}\\theta )]^{5} & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(5\\sqrt{5}\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(5\\sqrt{5}\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
